## General vGPU Restrictions

The following CUDA features are **not supported on vGPU** (per NVIDIA docs):

- CUDA-graphics API interoperability (OpenGL/DirectX ↔ CUDA memory sharing)
- GPUDirect RDMA
- Peer-to-peer GPU communication
- Dynamic page retirement
- **Reduced BAR1 memory** — partitioned across VMs, limits scene complexity

Any Omniverse feature that relies on these will fail in our environment. Before implementing features that use custom CUDA kernels or CUDA-graphics bridging, verify they work on vGPU. Be mindful of scene complexity to avoid BAR1 exhaustion.

